---
import { Code } from 'astro:components'
import Docs from '../layouts/Docs.astro'
import TokenTable from '../components/TokenTable.astro'

const install = `pnpm add @subfloor/core @subfloor/astro   # Astro
pnpm add @subfloor/core @subfloor/react   # React / Next.js`

const css = `/* Once, in the global stylesheet or layout */
@import '@subfloor/core/tokens.css';
@import '@subfloor/core/components.css';`

const tailwind = `/* With Tailwind v4: the mapping first, so its layer order applies */
@import '@subfloor/core/tailwind.css';
@import 'tailwindcss';
@import '@subfloor/core/tokens.css';
@import '@subfloor/core/components.css';`
---

<Docs
  title="Subfloor"
  description="The layer under the visible design: overlays that do not let the page scroll behind them, keep focus where it belongs and work before JavaScript arrives."
>
  <h2>Principles</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Native first.</strong> <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> with{' '}
      <code>showModal()</code>, Invoker Commands, <code>:has()</code>,{' '}
      <code>dvh</code>, <code>overscroll-behavior</code>. A little TypeScript
      only where the platform falls short: the iOS scroll lock, exit
      transitions,
      <code>data-state</code>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>One core, thin adapters.</strong> Behaviour and CSS live in{' '}
      <code>@subfloor/core</code>;<code>@subfloor/react</code> and{' '}
      <code>@subfloor/astro</code> only render its markup.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Customise without forking.</strong> Every visual value is a token;
      all kit CSS is in
      <code>@layer subfloor</code>, so your CSS and utility classes win without
      <code>!important</code>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Install</h2>
  <Code code={install} lang="sh" />
  <Code code={css} lang="css" />
  <Code code={tailwind} lang="css" />

  <h2>Components</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <a href="/modal/">Modal</a>: a centred dialog.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/drawer/">Drawer and Sheet</a>: the same dialog along an edge or
      from the bottom.
    </li>
    <li>
      <a href="/react/">React adapter</a>: the same components in React (Next.js
      App Router).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tokens</h2>
  <p>
    Defaults below; dark values apply under{' '}
    <code>prefers-color-scheme: dark</code>. Override any of them on{' '}
    <code>:root</code>, a wrapper or one component.
  </p>
  <TokenTable />
</Docs>
